2026-11-18T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A ZFS pool written raw to a BDXL disc
 # uuid: 50d1e693-331b-57fa-b210-e85270c9168d
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-18T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2498) 'a 100 GB BDXL archive is an encrypted ZFS pool image written to the disc raw.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2498) 'the encrypted archive image that is written raw to a 100 GB BDXL disc and its contents.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Can a 100 GB BDXL disc hold an encrypted ZFS pool with no filesystem of its own, and how many bytes of files does that leave room for?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A disc normally carries a UDF filesystem, which takes space and hides the blocks from ZFS. Written raw to a blank disc, the pool image fills the whole raw capacity of about 100.1 billion bytes, and ZFS reads the disc device itself. ZFS still keeps about 3% of the pool free, so the files get about 96.7 GB.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Read the section "Layout and budget" for the measured counts. The check passes when the disc is read back to the same hash as the image, the pool imports from the disc read-only and its files match the budget.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Layout and budget for a raw BDXL archive
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A BDXL archive is one ZFS pool image of 100,103,356,416 bytes with native encryption, written raw to a blank disc, with one dataset per file set and at most 96,500,000,000 bytes of files.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The pool's one disk is a file with the 4096-byte sector shift of RFD66606-2496 (ZFS data disks). It encrypts with aes-256-gcm and compresses every dataset with zstd.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Each file set is one dataset named for the set, and files keep their names and paths.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2498) '- ZFS block checksums replace a separate checksum list. The pool is exported before the image is written, and the disc is never mounted or formatted.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The disc holds one copy of each block, so only a second disc repairs a damaged one.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The image size is the disc's raw capacity, a multiple of 4096 bytes. The burn is refused when the blank disc reports fewer blocks than the image holds.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The passphrase is a fresh 24-word BIP39 seed phrase, never a wallet seed. The agent makes it, pipes it to the pool and stores it in 1Password and the keychain (operator, 2026-11-18).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2498) '- A file set is stored as an encrypted dataset with its own passphrase on a data pool such as FIRE202610, and archived by copying it into the disc's pool (operator, 2026-11-18).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2498) '- An M-DISC BDXL disc counts as the same capacity as a BD-R XL disc until a blank one has been read in a drive.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2498) '- RFD66606-2496 (ZFS data disks), the pool options this archive inherits.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Layout and budget
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The raw capacity of a triple-layer BD-R XL disc is 100,103,356,416 bytes, which is 48,878,592 logical sectors of 2048 bytes. The figure is listed for BD-R XL and BD-RE XL on the Wikipedia page for recordable Blu-ray discs, and the multiplication checks out. The ISO standard for these discs and the Blu-ray Disc Association paper give only the rounded 100 GB, so the exact figure rests on that page and on burning tools that report real discs. A raw write needs no UDF space and no formatting, so the image may use all of it. A disc that was formatted with defect management first would hold 256 MiB less.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A trial on the Mac made a pool of exactly that size on a file, with OpenZFS 2.3.1 and the options below. The pool reported 99,857,989,632 bytes, and the top dataset offered 96,753,676,288 bytes to files, because ZFS holds back a share of the pool as slop space. A scrub found no errors, and the exported pool imported read-only from the file and loaded its key. The 96,500,000,000-byte budget keeps about 253 MB of that offer in reserve. The trial did not write to a disc, so the raw write and the read from a disc device are untested.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Making the pool image
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The options follow RFD66606-2496, with encryption added and a mount point under /Volumes. The properties normalization, casesensitivity and utf8only cannot be changed after creation. The trial used a key file in place of the passphrase prompt. Set the four variables first. IMG is an absolute path, because a file disk needs one. The passphrase never goes in a variable: the pool prompts for it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2498) '```sh
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2498) 'export ZBIN=/usr/local/zfs/bin POOL=NAME SET=<set> IMG=/abs/path/NAME.img
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2498) 'truncate -s 100103356416 "$IMG"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2498) 'sudo "$ZBIN/zpool" create -f \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -o ashift=12 \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -O encryption=aes-256-gcm -O keyformat=passphrase -O keylocation=prompt \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -O compression=zstd -O atime=off -O copies=1 \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -O normalization=formD -O casesensitivity=insensitive -O utf8only=on \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -O mountpoint="/Volumes/$POOL" \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2498) '  "$POOL" "$IMG"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2498) 'sudo "$ZBIN/zfs" create "$POOL/$SET"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2498) 'sudo "$ZBIN/zpool" scrub -w "$POOL"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2498) 'sudo "$ZBIN/zpool" export "$POOL"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2498) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The passphrase reaches the prompt on standard input, so no variable or history line holds it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The image file is on the internal APFS volume. On the Mac, a file disk on the FIRE202610 ZFS pool failed with "no such device in pool", and the same create on APFS ran.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Autoexpand stays off, so the pool never grows past the image.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Compression is zstd on the pool and every dataset inherits it. No dataset sets it to off or to another algorithm, because the setting is part of what the checks read back.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2498) '- A scrub needs a writable pool, so it runs before the export and not on the disc.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Store and archive
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Native encryption is per dataset, so the data pool stays unencrypted and each file set is one encrypted dataset: `zfs create -o encryption=aes-256-gcm -o keyformat=passphrase -o keylocation=prompt POOL/SET`. Names, sizes and properties of datasets stay readable without the key, and file contents, names and paths do not. The archive copies the stored dataset into the disc's pool. Whether a raw `zfs send` keeps the stored key or the disc pool's key governs the copy is untested, so the first archive records which tool was used.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Writing the disc
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The first burn tests the write path, so record which tool and flags worked. The candidate on the Mac is `xorriso -as cdrecord`, which writes a raw data track from an image file. Read the blank disc's reported block count first and refuse the burn when it is under 48,878,592. After the write, read the whole disc back and hash it against the image.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The passphrase
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The passphrase is a 24-word BIP39 seed phrase, which carries 256 bits. The agent draws 32 random bytes, appends the 8 checksum bits and maps each 11 bits to a word of the list, then stores the phrase in 1Password and the login keychain without printing it. The operator may also keep it on paper apart from the disc. The pool takes the words themselves, lowercase and separated by single spaces, as the passphrase, piped from the keychain to the prompt. The pool derives no wallet seed from the words. The word list is the attachment `bip39_english.txt` in this RFD's apparatus directory, with its source and license in the `NOTICE.md` beside it. The agent recomputes the checksum bits from the stored phrase before the pool is made, and reads the keychain and 1Password entries back to the same words.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Checks
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Capacity: the blank disc reports at least 48,878,592 blocks, and a blank M-DISC BDXL disc is read in a drive and compared with the raw figure above.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Compression: `zfs get -r compression NAME` reads zstd on the pool and on every dataset, run before the export.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Budget: the files total at most 96,500,000,000 bytes, read from the datasets' used space.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Readback: the whole disc reads back to the same SHA-256 as the image.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Import: the pool imports from the disc device read-only, the key loads, and the files open.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Cross host: the same disc imports on Linux and Windows with OpenZFS.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written
